 "executable_help": "Serve a local package or download a prepared package from Hugging Face\n\nUsage: flare-public-4528c220 run [OPTIONS] <PACKAGE>\n\nArguments:\n  <PACKAGE>  Local prepared .safetensors package or Hugging Face ORG/NAME[@REVISION]\n\nOptions:\n      --publisher-keys <PATH>\n          Additional publisher verification profiles (JSON); does not grant execution trust. Development packages default to ~/.config/flare/development-publisher.json\n      --verify-weights\n          Verify stored allocation and table ranges before loading model GPU resources\n      --dangerously-approve-key <FINGERPRINT>\n          Permanently accept this exact signing key together with --dangerously-accept-publisher\n      --dangerously-accept-publisher <NAMESPACE>\n          Exact Hugging Face publisher namespace acknowledged for unattended first use\n      --trust-store <PATH>\n          Persistent trust file [default: ~/.config/flare/trust.toml]\n  -h, --help\n          Print help\n\nServing options:\n      --host <ADDR>\n          IP address for the HTTP server [default: 127.0.0.1]\n      --port <N>\n          Port for the HTTP server [default: 8000]\n      --served-model-name <ALIAS>\n          Replace the package's serving alias; the canonical model ID remains accepted\n      --api-key-file <PATH>\n          File containing the serving API key; omit to disable authentication\n      --scheduler-policy <MODE>\n          Favor token throughput, balance it with output cadence, or value agents' prompts closer to output; all retain token-service fairness [default: balanced] [possible values: balanced, throughput, agent]\n      --prefill-srpt\n          Serve concurrent prompts shortest-remaining-prompt first, one after another, instead of interleaving their prefill chunks [default: off]. Outputs and prefill arithmetic are unchanged\n      --prefill-srpt-max-wait-chunks <CHUNKS>\n          With --prefill-srpt: serve a prompt in arrival order once it has waited this many other prompts' prefill chunks; 0 removes the bound [default: 256]\n      --prefill-srpt-aging-tokens-per-chunk <TOKENS>\n          With --prefill-srpt: remaining-token credit per other prompt's prefill chunk waited [default: 32]\n      --unclamped-sampling\n          Validation only: accept request sampling values outside the package's model-author ranges, e.g. top_k 1 for greedy token-for-token comparisons. Not for serving\n      --gpus <N[,N...]>\n          GPUs in rank order, relative to CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES when set [default: 0]\n      --kv-cache-limit <MODE>\n          Limit KV capacity by available memory, one context, or context times concurrency [default: memory] [possible values: concurrency, context, memory]\n      --memory-limit <LIMIT>\n          Per-GPU serving memory: occupied size (30G), free reserve (-30G), or total fraction (0.8). Omitted: package serving reserve\n      --max-concurrency <N>\n          Maximum simultaneous requests [default: package setting]\n      --embedding-table-storage <MODE>\n          Storage for auxiliary embedding tables (PLE/Engram) [default: disk] [possible values: disk, ram]\n      --embedding-table-cache-size <SIZE>\n          Per-host budget for a disk-backed embedding row cache, e.g. 1G; includes the index, usage counters and miss workspace. Selects disk storage; 0 disables [default: 0] [default: 0]\n      --embedding-table-resident-scales\n          Retain embedding scales in host RAM while weights remain on disk; adds to the row-cache budget\n\nMulti-host options:\n      --roce-ring               Experimental ring in rank order: only neighbor RoCE QPs connect; native CPU relays forward non-neighbor traffic. Also emulates a ring on a switch\n      --rendezvous <HOST:PORT>  Rank zero's rendezvous address: where rank zero listens, or on a peer, where it joins rank zero\n      --rank <N>                This host's rank of a multi-host package\n\nSpeculation options:\n      --mtp-pipeline                  Queue the next speculative round behind the running one so graph submission overlaps execution; one local rank, device MTP proposals, no grammar or custom stops\n      --mtp-draft-tokens <N>          Maximum drafts per round; 0 disables speculation [default: package setting]\n      --mtp-adaptive-verification     Adapt verification width to acceptance estimates and execution cost [default: fixed width]. Adaptive rounds depend on batch composition, so sampled outputs then differ between concurrent and solo requests\n      --no-mtp-adaptive-verification  Use the maximum width where captured, otherwise width one [default]\n\nDownload options:\n      --revision <REVISION>  Hub revision; defaults to gb10 or gb202 detected from the selected GPUs\n      --filename <FILE>      Package filename; required when the revision contains several .safetensors files\n      --cache-dir <PATH>     Hugging Face hub cache [default: ~/.cache/huggingface/hub]\n      --token-file <PATH>    Hugging Face access token file; omit for public repositories\n      --offline              Use only cached files, without contacting Hugging Face\n\nAdvanced serving options:\n      --embedding-table-workers <N>  Disk workers per embedding table; shares a fixed I/O budget [default: 4 on Windows, 1 elsewhere] [possible values: 1, 2, 4, 8]\n\nAdvanced speculation options:\n      --mtp-verification-token-budget <N>\n          Advanced: fix the total verification-row budget, including pending inputs, using one exact captured packed graph per batch [default: adaptive within captured capacities]. Requires adaptive prefix selection at the captured draft depth\n      --mtp-max-verification-token-budget <N>\n          Advanced: retain all captured packed verification capacities up to N total rows, including pending inputs [default: all captured capacities]. Requires adaptive prefix selection at the captured draft depth\n\nPrefix cache options:\n      --prefix-cache-memory <SIZE>\n          Host memory for prefix checkpoints and prepared inputs, e.g. 16G; 0 disables [default: disabled]\n      --prefix-cache-disk <DIR>\n          Directory for prefix checkpoints and prepared inputs on disk [default: disabled]\n      --prefix-cache-disk-limit <SIZE>\n          Disk retention limit, e.g. 100G; 0 disables [default: 10% of free space]\n      --prefix-cache-disk-transport <MODE>\n          Transfer disk checkpoints through host staging or GPUDirect Storage [default: staged] [possible values: staged, direct]\n\nExamples:\n  flare run model.safetensors --gpus 0 --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000\n  flare run model.safetensors --embedding-table-storage ram --mtp-draft-tokens 3\n\nConcurrency and draft limits must fit the package's prepared capacities.\nOmitted concurrency and speculation options use package defaults.",
